                  "bodyEn": "Strategic classroom questioning transforms passive student listening into active, critical cognitive engagement.\n\nMary Budd Rowe's Wait-Time Research:\nExtending teacher wait-time from the typical 1 second to 3-5 seconds after asking a question produces profound academic benefits:\n- Student responses increase in length, syntactic complexity, and factual accuracy.\n- Failure to respond decreases dramatically.\n- Unsolicited but appropriate student contributions rise.\n- Students build upon and challenge peer ideas with reasoned evidence.\n\nSocratic Seminars:\n- Collaborative, text-based intellectual dialogues where students explore open-ended, complex questions.\n- Students sit in a circle without raised hands, practicing civil discourse, textual citation, and critical inquiry.",
