                  "bodyEn": "The derivative represents the fundamental mathematical concept of an instantaneous rate of change.\n\nFormal Limit Definition:\nf'(x) = lim (h -> 0) [f(x + h) - f(x)] / h\n\nFundamental Differentiation Rules:\n1. Power Rule: d/dx(x^n) = n * x^(n - 1)\n2. Product Rule: d/dx[u(x) * v(x)] = u'(x)v(x) + u(x)v'(x)\n3. Quotient Rule: d/dx[u(x) / v(x)] = [u'(x)v(x) - u(x)v'(x)] / [v(x)]^2\n4. Chain Rule: d/dx[f(g(x))] = f'(g(x)) * g'(x)\n\nReal-World Applications:\n- Physics: Instantaneous velocity v(t) = ds/dt and acceleration a(t) = dv/dt.\n- Economics: Marginal cost dC/dq and marginal revenue dR/dq optimization.\n- Computer Science & AI: Gradient descent optimization algorithms calculating partial derivatives of loss functions.",
