                  "bodyEn": "Multiple integrals compute volumes, masses, and fluxes over multi-dimensional geometric domains.\n\nDouble Integrals & Coordinate Transformations:\n∬_R f(x, y) dA represents the volume under the surface z = f(x, y) over region R.\nTransforming to Polar Coordinates (x = r cos θ, y = r sin θ):\n∬_R f(x, y) dx dy = ∬_D f(r cos θ, r sin θ) r dr dθ (where Jacobian determinant J = r).\n\nVector Calculus Operators:\nFor vector field F = [P, Q, R]:\n1. Divergence: div F = ∇ · F = ∂P/∂x + ∂Q/∂y + ∂R/∂z (measures net flux outflow per unit volume).\n2. Curl: curl F = ∇ × F (measures microscopic rotational circulation).\n\nGreen's Theorem in the Plane:\n∮_C (P dx + Q dy) = ∬_D (∂Q/∂x - ∂P/∂y) dA",
