                  "bodyEn": "Linear algebra provides the mathematical backbone of modern scientific computing, data science, and quantum mechanics.\n\nAxiomatic Vector Space:\nA set V over a field F closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication satisfying 8 fundamental axioms (associativity, commutativity, additive identity, zero element, distributivity).\n\nLinear Combinations & Independence:\n- A set of vectors {v1, v2, ..., vn} is linearly independent if the only solution to:\n  c1*v1 + c2*v2 + ... + cn*vn = 0 is c1 = c2 = ... = cn = 0.\n- If non-zero scalars exist that satisfy the equation, the vectors are linearly dependent.\n\nBasis and Dimension:\n- A Basis B for vector space V is a set of vectors that is both linearly independent and spans V.\n- The Dimension dim(V) is the unique number of vectors in any basis of V.",
