                  "bodyEn": "Matrices represent linear maps between finite-dimensional vector spaces.\n\nMatrix Operations:\n1. Matrix Multiplication: For matrices A (m × k) and B (k × n), product C = AB has dimensions m × n where:\n   c_ij = ∑ (a_il * b_lj) for l = 1 to k. Matrix multiplication is associative but strictly non-commutative (AB ≠ BA in general).\n2. The Determinant det(A): A scalar quantity encoding the geometric scaling factor of the transformation:\n   - det(A) = 0 if and only if matrix A is singular (non-invertible).\n   - For 2×2 matrix [a, b; c, d], det(A) = ad - bc.\n   - det(AB) = det(A) * det(B).\n\nMatrix Inversion:\nFor a non-singular square matrix A:\nA * A^(-1) = A^(-1) * A = I (Identity Matrix)\nComputed via Gaussian elimination [A | I] -> [I | A^(-1)] or the adjugate formula: A^(-1) = (1/det(A)) * adj(A).",
