                  "bodyEn": "Eigen-decomposition reveals the invariant directional axes of linear transformations.\n\nFundamental Eigenvalue Equation:\nA * v = λ * v (where v ≠ 0)\n- v is an eigenvector.\n- λ is the corresponding scalar eigenvalue.\n\nComputation via Characteristic Polynomial:\n(A - λI)v = 0\nFor non-trivial solutions v ≠ 0, the matrix (A - λI) must be singular:\ndet(A - λI) = 0\nSolving this polynomial yields the eigenvalues λ1, λ2, ..., λn.\n\nMatrix Diagonalization:\nIf an n × n matrix A has n linearly independent eigenvectors, it can be factored as:\nA = P * D * P^(-1)\nWhere P is the matrix of eigenvectors and D is the diagonal matrix of corresponding eigenvalues.\nKey Applications: Principal Component Analysis (PCA), PageRank algorithms, and solving coupled systems of differential equations.",
