                  "bodyEn": "Differential equations express relationships between functions and their derivatives, modeling dynamic systems across nature.\n\nFirst-Order ODE Standard Form:\ndy/dx = f(x, y)\n\nAnalytical Solution Methods:\n1. Separable Equations: Expressible as g(y) dy = h(x) dx; solved by direct integration on both sides:\n   ∫ g(y) dy = ∫ h(x) dx + C.\n2. First-Order Linear ODEs: dy/dx + P(x)y = Q(x)\n   - Solved using the Integrating Factor method: μ(x) = exp(∫ P(x) dx).\n   - Multiplying through yields: d/dx[μ(x)y] = μ(x)Q(x).\n   - Solution: y(x) = [1/μ(x)] * [ ∫ μ(x)Q(x) dx + C ].\n3. Exact Equations: M(x, y) dx + N(x, y) dy = 0 where ∂M/∂y = ∂N/∂x.",
