                  "bodyEn": "Faiz Ahmad Faiz (1911–1984) is universally celebrated for synthesizing classical poetic beauty with Marxist political resistance.\n\nKey Hallmarks of Faiz's Poetry:\n1. Re-purposing Classical Imagery: Traditional romantic tropes (the beloved, the cage, the executioner) are elevated into political symbols:\n   - Mehboob (محبوب): The Beloved becomes a metaphor for the motherland, freedom, and universal humanity.\n   - Zindaan (زنداں) & Qafas (قفس): The prison cell symbolizes imperialist and dictatorial tyranny.\n2. Musical Melodiousness (غنائیت): Retained sublime rhythmic elegance and tenderness even when articulating fierce political defiance.\n3. Masterpieces: \"Mujh Se Pehli Si Mohabbat\", \"Subh-e-Azadi\", \"Bol Ke Lab Azaad Hain Tere\", and \"Hum Dekhenge\".",
