              "sections": [
                {
                  "heading": "Academic Lecture Notes & Analytical Framework",
                  "urduHeading": "علمی نوٹس اور فکری جائزہ",
                  "bodyEn": "Data structures organize data in physical memory to maximize operational efficiency and spatial cache locality.\n\nLinear Data Structures:\n1. Arrays (Contiguous Memory):\n   - Fast random access: O(1) time via base address + (index * element_size).\n   - Costly insertions/deletions: O(n) time due to shifting adjacent elements.\n2. Linked Lists (Node-Pointer Chains):\n   - Dynamic sizing with fast insertion/deletion at known nodes: O(1) pointer updates.\n   - Slow random access: O(n) sequential traversal; poor CPU cache line spatial locality.\n3. Stacks (LIFO - Last In, First Out):\n   - Fundamental operations: push(), pop(), peek() - all guaranteed O(1).\n   - Use cases: Compiler call stacks, syntax parsing, undo/redo buffers.\n4. Queues (FIFO - First In, First Out):\n   - Operations: enqueue(), dequeue() - O(1) via head/tail pointers.\n   - Use cases: CPU task scheduling, print spooling, Breadth-First Search (BFS).",
                  "bodyUrdu": ""
                }
              ],
