              "sections": [
                {
                  "heading": "Academic Lecture Notes & Analytical Framework",
                  "urduHeading": "علمی نوٹس اور فکری جائزہ",
                  "bodyEn": "Non-linear hierarchical data structures facilitate fast logarithmic searching, sorting, and priority routing.\n\nTree Terminology & Binary Search Trees (BST):\n- BST Property: For every node N, all keys in the left subtree are strictly less than N.key, and all keys in the right subtree are strictly greater.\n- Traversal Orders: Pre-order (Node-L-R), In-order (L-Node-R yields sorted keys), Post-order (L-R-Node).\n- Balanced BSTs (AVL & Red-Black Trees): Enforce balance criteria through tree rotations, guaranteeing worst-case O(log n) search, insertion, and deletion.\n\nBinary Heaps & Priority Queues:\n- Complete Binary Tree stored compactly in a flat array (Node at index i has children at 2i + 1 and 2i + 2).\n- Heap Property: In a Max-Heap, parent key ≥ children keys.\n- Heapify Operation: Restores heap invariant in O(log n) time.\n- Heap Sort: Sorts an array of length n in guaranteed O(n log n) time in-place.",
                  "bodyUrdu": ""
                }
              ],
