                  "bodyEn": "Development economics explores how emerging nations escape systemic poverty and achieve sustainable prosperity.\n\nModern Paradigms of Development:\n1. Amartya Sen's Capabilities Approach: Development is defined not merely by GDP growth, but by the expansion of real human freedoms and capabilities (access to healthcare, literacy, political voice, and longevity).\n2. Institutional Economics (Daron Acemoglu & James Robinson - \"Why Nations Fail\"):\n   - Extractive Institutions: Concentrate political and economic power in elite oligarchies, expropriating wealth and stifling innovation.\n   - Inclusive Institutions: Secure property rights, enforce an impartial rule of law, and encourage broad-based investment, sustaining economic flourishing.\n3. Poverty Traps: Self-reinforcing cycles where low income leads to malnutrition and lack of schooling, depressing productivity and perpetuating generational deprivation.",
