                  "bodyEn": "Rotational dynamics parallels translational mechanics through angular analogs.\n\nRotational Mechanical Analogs:\n- Translational Mass (m) <-> Moment of Inertia (I = ∑ m_i * r_i² = ∫ r² dm): Quantifies rotational resistance to angular acceleration.\n- Force (F) <-> Torque (τ = r × F = I * α): The rotational twisting force about a pivot axis.\n- Momentum (p = mv) <-> Angular Momentum (L = r × p = I * ω).\n\nConservation of Angular Momentum:\nWhen net external torque on a system is zero (∑ τ_ext = 0), total angular momentum remains strictly conserved: I_initial * ω_initial = I_final * ω_final (demonstrated by a spinning figure skater pulling in their arms to reduce I, causing angular velocity ω to increase).",
