                  "bodyEn": "Simple Harmonic Motion (SHM) occurs whenever an oscillating entity experiences a restoring force directly proportional to its displacement from equilibrium.\n\nMathematical Dynamics of SHM:\n- Hooke's Law: F = -k * x\n- Differential Equation: d²x/dt² + (k/m)x = 0  ->  d²x/dt² + ω²x = 0 (where natural angular frequency ω = √(k/m)).\n- General Solution: x(t) = A * cos(ωt + φ), where A is Amplitude and φ is Phase Constant.\n- Period of Oscillation: T = 2π / ω = 2π √(m/k).\n- Simple Pendulum (Small Angle Approximation θ < 15°): T = 2π √(L/g).\n\nResonance:\nWhen an oscillating system is driven by a periodic external force matching its natural resonance frequency (ω_drive ≈ ω_0), oscillation amplitude increases dramatically.",
