                  "bodyEn": "Mechanical waves propagate energy and momentum through a deformable physical medium without transporting bulk matter.\n\nWave Classifications:\n1. Transverse Waves: Particle oscillation is perpendicular to wave propagation (light, electromagnetic waves, seismic S-waves).\n2. Longitudinal Waves: Particle oscillation is parallel to wave propagation, forming alternating Compressions and Rarefactions (acoustic sound waves, seismic P-waves).\n\nThe Universal Wave Equation: v = f * λ (Wave Speed = Frequency × Wavelength).\n\nThe Doppler Effect:\nThe observed shift in frequency resulting from relative motion between a wave source and an observer: f' = f * [ (v ± v_observer) / (v ∓ v_source) ]. Moving toward each other compresses wavelengths, causing high-pitch blue-shift; moving apart elongates wavelengths, causing low-pitch red-shift.",
