                  "bodyEn": "Electrostatics examines the forces, electric fields, and potentials generated by stationary electric charges.\n\nCoulomb's Law:\nF = (1 / 4πε0) * (|q1 * q2| / r²)\nWhere ε0 is the Permittivity of Free Space (ε0 ≈ 8.854 × 10⁻¹² C² / N · m²).\n\nGauss's Law for Electricity (Maxwell's First Equation):\n∮ E · dA = Q_enclosed / ε0\nThe net electric flux through any closed Gaussian surface is directly proportional to the total enclosed charge, providing elegant solutions for spherical, cylindrical, and planar symmetries.\n\nElectric Potential (V) & Capacitance (C):\n- Electric Potential: V = -∫ E · dr (Scalar potential field measured in Volts).\n- Capacitance: C = Q / V. For parallel-plate capacitors: C = ε * (A / d), storing electrostatic potential energy: U = (1/2)C*V².",
