                  "bodyEn": "Electric circuits channel direct current (DC) flow through networks of resistors, voltage sources, and reactive components.\n\nOhm's Law & Resistor Networks:\n- V = I * R (Voltage = Current × Resistance).\n- Series Resistors: R_eq = R1 + R2 + ... (current is identical through each).\n- Parallel Resistors: 1/R_eq = 1/R1 + 1/R2 + ... (voltage is identical across each).\n\nKirchhoff's Circuit Laws:\n1. Kirchhoff's Current Law (KCL - Junction Rule): Total current entering any electrical junction must precisely equal total current leaving (Conservation of Charge): ∑ I_in = ∑ I_out.\n2. Kirchhoff's Voltage Law (KVL - Loop Rule): The algebraic sum of all potential differences around any closed circuit loop must equal zero (Conservation of Energy): ∑ ΔV = 0.\n\nRC Transient Charging Dynamics:\nV(t) = V0 * (1 - e^(-t / RC)), where τ = RC is the circuit Time Constant.",
