                  "bodyEn": "Magnetic fields are generated exclusively by moving electric charges and intrinsic quantum electron spins.\n\nThe Lorentz Force Equation:\nF = q * (E + v × B)\nA charged particle moving through a magnetic field experiences a deflecting force perpendicular to both its velocity vector and the magnetic field lines (Right-Hand Rule).\n\nMagnetic Field Generation:\n1. The Biot-Savart Law: Infinitesimal current element generates magnetic field: dB = (μ0 / 4π) * (I dl × r̂ / r²).\n2. Ampère's Circuital Law: ∮ B · dl = μ0 * I_enclosed (for steady currents).\n3. Field of an Ideal Solenoid: B = μ0 * n * I (where n is turns per unit length), generating an intense, uniform interior magnetic field.",
