                  "bodyEn": "Electromagnetic induction is the physical phenomenon underpinning all modern electrical generators, transformers, and induction motors.\n\nFaraday's Law of Induction:\nAn induced Electromotive Force (EMF - ε) is generated in any closed circuit loop when the magnetic flux passing through that loop changes over time:\nε = -dΦ_B / dt  (where magnetic flux Φ_B = ∬ B · dA).\n\nLenz's Law (The Negative Sign):\nThe polarity of an induced EMF generates an electric current whose magnetic field strictly OPPOSES the original change in magnetic flux that produced it (Conservation of Energy).\n\nMutual Inductance & Electrical Transformers:\nV_secondary / V_primary = N_secondary / N_primary = I_primary / I_secondary, stepping voltages up or down with minimal resistive thermal dissipation.",
