                  "bodyEn": "Atomic physics models the electronic shell architecture surrounding atomic nuclei.\n\nEvolution of the Atomic Model:\n1. Rutherford Alpha Scattering Experiment (1911): Fired alpha particles at thin gold foil; rare wide-angle backscattering revealed that the atom is mostly empty space with a tiny, dense, positively charged nucleus.\n2. The Bohr Model of Hydrogen (Niels Bohr, 1913): Postulated that electrons inhabit discrete, non-radiating quantized orbits where angular momentum is quantized: L = n * ℏ.\n   - Energy Levels of Hydrogen: E_n = -13.6 eV / n².\n   - Atomic Line Spectra: Photons are emitted or absorbed when electrons transition between quantized energy tiers: ΔE = E_initial - E_final = h * f (explaining Lyman, Balmer, and Paschen spectral series).\n3. Quantum Mechanical Orbital Model: Solves the 3D Schrödinger equation to yield Quantum Numbers: Principal (n), Azimuthal (l), Magnetic (m_l), and Spin (m_s).",
