                  "bodyEn": "Stereochemistry investigates the 3D spatial arrangement of atoms within isomeric molecules.\n\nChirality & Enantiomerism:\n- Chiral Carbon (Stereocenter): An sp³ hybridized carbon atom bonded to four distinctly different substituent groups.\n- Enantiomers: Non-superimposable mirror image stereoisomers: Possess identical physical properties (melting point, density), but rotate plane-polarized light in equal and opposite directions (+ dextrorotatory, - levorotatory; Optical Activity).\n- Diastereomers: Stereoisomers that are not mirror images (e.g., cis/trans alkenes; differing at some but not all chiral centers); exhibit distinctly different physical and chemical properties.\n\nCahn-Ingold-Prelog (CIP) Priority Rules:\nSubstituents are prioritized by atomic number (Z). Viewing with lowest priority (#4) pointing away: clockwise sequence 1->2->3 is designated (R) (Rectus); counter-clockwise is designated (S) (Sinister).",
