                  "bodyEn": "Polymers are high-molecular-weight macromolecules synthesized by linking repeating chemical units termed Monomers.\n\nPolymerization Mechanisms:\n1. Addition (Chain-Growth) Polymerization: Monomers containing carbon-carbon double bonds link without loss of small molecules (Initiation, Propagation, Termination):\n   - Polyethylene (plastic bags), Polypropylene, Polystyrene, Polyvinyl Chloride (PVC).\n2. Condensation (Step-Growth) Polymerization: Bi-functional monomers react with the elimination of small byproduct molecules (typically water or HCl):\n   - Nylon 6,6 (polyamide synthesized from adipic acid and hexamethylenediamine), Dacron (polyester).\n\nPhysical Properties & Cross-Linking:\n- Thermoplastics: Linear or branched polymers that melt reversibly upon heating.\n- Thermosets: Heavily cross-linked covalent networks that degrade rather than melt upon heating (bakelite, vulcanized rubber).",
