                  "bodyEn": "Environmental chemistry investigates chemical species in the environment and the technological design of sustainable industrial processes.\n\nStratospheric Ozone Depletion:\n- The Chapman Cycle naturally balances stratospheric ozone formation and destruction.\n- Catalytic Destruction by Chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs): Solar UV photolysis releases free Chlorine radicals (Cl·), which catalyze the destruction of ozone molecules:\n  Cl· + O3 -> ClO· + O2\n  ClO· + O· -> Cl· + O2\n  Net Reaction: O3 + O· -> 2 O2 (A single chlorine radical destroys over 100,000 ozone molecules before termination).\n\nThe 12 Principles of Green Chemistry (Anastas & Warner):\nAtom Economy (maximizing incorporation of all raw materials into final product), prevention of waste, using safer solvents, designing for degradation, and catalytic rather than stoichiometric reagents.",
