              "sections": [
                {
                  "heading": "Academic Lecture Notes & Analytical Framework",
                  "urduHeading": "علمی نوٹس اور فکری جائزہ",
                  "bodyEn": "Modifiers are words, phrases, or clauses that furnish descriptive detail about another sentence component.\n\nCategories of Modification Errors:\n1. Misplaced Modifiers: Positioned too far from the noun they modify, creating absurd interpretations.\n   - Error: \"The professor served tea to the students in porcelain cups.\" (Were the students in cups?).\n   - Correction: \"The professor served tea in porcelain cups to the students.\"\n2. Dangling Modifiers: An introductory modifier whose intended subject is entirely missing from the main clause.\n   - Error: \"Having finished the experiment, the results were compiled.\"\n   - Correction: \"Having finished the experiment, the team compiled the results.\"\n3. Squinting Modifiers: An adverb positioned ambiguously between two elements such that it could logically modify either.\n   - Error: \"Students who exercise frequently achieve higher examination scores.\" (Do they exercise frequently, or frequently achieve scores?).\n   - Correction: \"Students who frequently exercise achieve higher scores.\"",
                  "bodyUrdu": ""
                }
              ],
