              "sections": [
                {
                  "heading": "Academic Lecture Notes & Analytical Framework",
                  "urduHeading": "علمی نوٹس اور فکری جائزہ",
                  "bodyEn": "Corpus linguistics utilizes vast digitized databases of authentic written and spoken texts to empirically investigate language patterns.\n\nMethodological Tools in Corpus Linguistics:\n1. Concordance Lines (KWIC - Key Word in Context): Displays hundreds of authentic textual occurrences of a target word aligned horizontally, revealing common collocational partners.\n2. Collocations: Words that co-occur with a frequency significantly greater than random chance (e.g., in English we say \"commit a crime\" rather than \"perform a crime\"; \"heavy rain\" rather than \"dense rain\").\n3. N-Grams: Continuous sequences of n items from a text (unigrams, bigrams, trigrams) used in natural language processing (NLP) to model linguistic probability.\n\nDescriptive vs Prescriptive Lexicography:\n- Prescriptive Approach: Dictates how people \"ought\" to speak based on historical or Latinate rules.\n- Descriptive Approach: Catalogs how native speakers actually use living language in authentic communication.",
                  "bodyUrdu": ""
                }
              ],
