                  "bodyEn": "Mary Shelley's \"Frankenstein\" (1818) launched modern science fiction and redefined Gothic horror through philosophical inquiry.\n\nThe Myth of Prometheus & Scientific Hubris:\n- The Subtitle: Prometheus stole divine fire from the Olympian gods, suffering eternal punishment. Victor Frankenstein usurps divine biological creation, seeking to vanquish death through empirical natural philosophy.\n- The Creature as Noble Savage: Influenced by Jean-Jacques Rousseau, the creature is born benevolent and longing for affection; society's violent rejection of his grotesque visage corrupts him into vengeance.\n- The Romantic Sublime: The desolate glacial landscapes of Mont Blanc and the Arctic ice fields reflect the overwhelming, terrifying indifference of nature against human vanity.",
