                  "bodyEn": "On March 23, 1940, at Minto Park (now Iqbal Park) in Lahore, the All-India Muslim League formally adopted the historic Lahore Resolution (Qarardad-e-Lahore).\n\nKey Provisions of the Resolution:\n- Moved by Bengal Premier A.K. Fazlul Huq and seconded by leaders across all provinces.\n- Resolved: \"No constitutional plan would be workable in this country or acceptable to the Muslims unless it is designed on the following basic principle, viz., that geographically contiguous units are demarcated into regions... in which the Muslims are numerically in a majority as in the North-Western and Eastern zones of India, should be grouped to constitute 'Independent States' in which the constituent units shall be autonomous and sovereign.\"\n\nThe Two-Nation Theory Articulated by Quaid-e-Azam:\nIn his presidential address, Jinnah declared:\n\"Hindus and Muslims belong to two different religious philosophies, social customs, and literatures. They neither intermarry nor interdine together, and indeed, they belong to two different civilizations which are based mainly on conflicting ideas and conceptions.\"",
                  "bodyUrdu": ""
