                  "bodyEn": "The Cold War (1947–1991) was an ideological, geopolitical, and nuclear confrontation between the capitalist United States and the communist Soviet Union.\n\nDynamics of Nuclear Brinkmanship:\n- Mutually Assured Destruction (MAD): Massive nuclear arsenals deterred direct military conflict between superpowers.\n- Containment & The Truman Doctrine: US commitment to prevent the global spread of communism.\n- The Berlin Wall: Erected in 1961 by East Germany to halt defection to the West, standing as the supreme concrete symbol of the Iron Curtain.\n- The Cuban Missile Crisis (October 1962): The closest humanity came to full-scale thermonuclear war, resolved when Soviet missiles were removed from Cuba in exchange for US pledges not to invade Cuba and removal of US missiles from Turkey.\n- The Dissolution: Mikhail Gorbachev's reforms (Glasnost - openness, Perestroika - restructuring) led to the fall of the Berlin Wall (1989) and dissolution of the USSR (1991).",
