              "sections": [
                {
                  "heading": "Academic Lecture Notes & Analytical Framework",
                  "urduHeading": "علمی نوٹس اور فکری جائزہ",
                  "bodyEn": "Karl Marx (1818–1883) formulated Historical Materialism, asserting that economic productive forces drive all human history.\n\nBase and Superstructure Architecture:\n- The Economic Base: The Forces of Production (machinery, raw materials, labor) and Relations of Production (property ownership, employment contracts).\n- The Superstructure: Legal systems, religion, political states, philosophy, and media—which exist to legitimize and reproduce the economic interests of the ruling class.\n\nMarx's Four Dimensions of Alienation (Entfremdung):\nUnder capitalist wage labor, the worker is alienated from: (1) The product of labor, (2) The act of production, (3) Human species-essence (Gattungswesen / creative potential), and (4) Fellow human beings.\n\nFalse Consciousness vs Class Consciousness:\nWorkers are kept compliant through \"False Consciousness\" (ideologies like religion being the \"opium of the people\"), until organizing into collective revolutionary \"Class Consciousness\".",
                  "bodyUrdu": ""
                }
              ],
